  "changes": [
    {
      "kind": "minor",
      "description": "Accepts a street network and draws it as itself. Four widgets consumed a network port -- isochrone, reachable_corridor, reachable_nodes, snap_to_network -- and none of them was an output, so a downloaded graph had no way to be looked at: the only feedback was a node and edge count, and the only real check was to run an isochrone over it and judge the answer. A new input mode rather than a new always-present port, following raster and polygons, so nothing changes for a Map that shows points. Emits fw:networkJunctionCount and fw:networkSegmentCount; it routes nothing, simplifies nothing and infers nothing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "minor",
      "description": "Standalone map title, subtitle, key and source note, SVG export, and selectable local/OSM/OpenTopoMap basemaps for interactive polygons."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "status": "not-individually-certified",
